{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-vm.k | sed -n '1,165p'; nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-ext.k | sed -n '107,160p'; rg -n 'fn main|parse.*Fr|from_str|inputs|read_to_string' /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_build/ledger-92e8bdd3/zkir*/src/bin/zkir-oracle.rs; nl -ba /home/charl/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/midnight-circuits-7.2.4/src/ecc/hash_to_curve/htc_gadget.rs | sed -n '62,95p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// ZKIR v3 virtual machine: the witness computation (`IrSource::preprocess`,\n     2\t// zkir-v3/src/ir_vm.rs at midnight-ledger 92e8bdd3) and, in the same rewrite,\n     3\t// the constraint set that `Relation::circuit` would synthesise for the same\n     4\t// instruction (plan decisions CLM-0704 .. CLM-0706, CLM-0720).\n     5\t//\n     6\t// State (one cell per component of the seven-tuple on the VM wiki page):\n     7\t//   <mem>        registers, String |-> Value, write-once\n     8\t//   <pi>         public-input vector (binding input, optional commitment, impacts)\n     9\t//   <skips>      pi_skips: skipNone() for an active impact, skipSome(n) for an inactive one\n    10\t//   <pubInIdx>, <pubOutIdx>, <privIdx>   transcript cursors\n    11\t//   <outputs>    values returned by `output`, in order\n    12\t//   <constraints> instruction-level relations emitted by every instruction,\n    13\t//                whether or not the witness computation is still alive\n    14\t//   <status>     ok() or error(msg): the first witness failure freezes the\n    15\t//                witness cells; the remaining instructions still emit constraints\n    16\t//\n    17\t// A run is job(program, preimage). The preimage mirrors `ProofPreimage`.\n    18\trequires \"zkir-syntax.k\"\n    19\trequires \"zkir-ops.k\"\n    20\trequires \"zkir-constraints.k\"\n    21\t\n    22\tmodule ZKIR-VM-SYNTAX\n    23\t  imports ZKIR-SYNTAX\n    24\t  imports LIST\n    25\t  imports INT\n    26\t\n    27\t  syntax Preimage ::= preimage(List, Int, CommOpt, List, List, List) [symbol(preimage)]\n    28\t                      // inputs, binding_input, communications_commitment, private_transcript,\n    29\t                      // public_transcript_inputs, public_transcript_outputs\n    30\t  syntax CommOpt  ::= noComm()        [symbol(noComm)]\n    31\t                    | comm(Int, Int)  [symbol(comm)]    // (commitment, opening randomness)\n    32\t  syntax Job ::= job(Program, Preimage)    [symbol(job)]\n    33\t               | genJob(Program, Preimage) [symbol(genJob)]   // generation mode, see <genMode>\n    34\tendmodule\n    35\t\n    36\tmodule ZKIR-VM\n    37\t  imports ZKIR-VM-SYNTAX\n    38\t  imports ZKIR-WF\n    39\t  imports ZKIR-OPS\n    40\t  imports ZKIR-CONSTRAINTS\n    41\t  imports MAP\n    42\t  imports SET\n    43\t  imports K-EQUAL\n    44\t\n    45\t  syntax Status ::= ok() [symbol(ok)] | error(String) [symbol(error)]\n    46\t  syntax Skip   ::= skipNone() [symbol(skipNone)] | skipSome(Int) [symbol(skipSome)]\n    47\t\n    48\t  // Constraints (sort Constraint, ZKIR-CONSTRAINTS): the in-circuit relation\n    49\t  // of one instruction over register names and immediates; piGate(i, g, x)\n    50\t  // states pi[i] = g ? x : 0; piFixed pins the binding input and commitment.\n    51\t\n    52\t  configuration\n    53\t    <zkir>\n    54\t      <k> $PGM:Job </k>\n    55\t      <mem> .Map </mem>\n    56\t      <pi> .List </pi>\n    57\t      <skips> .List </skips>\n    58\t      <pubInIdx> 0 </pubInIdx>\n    59\t      <pubOutIdx> 0 </pubOutIdx>\n    60\t      <privIdx> 0 </privIdx>\n    61\t      <outputs> .List </outputs>\n    62\t      <outTypes> .IrTypes </outTypes>\n    63\t      <doComm> false </doComm>\n    64\t      <pre> preimage(.List, 0, noComm(), .List, .List, .List) </pre>\n    65\t      <constraints> .List </constraints>\n    66\t      <chips> .Set </chips>\n    67\t      <verdicts> .List </verdicts>\n    68\t      <deadPis> 0 </deadPis>\n    69\t      <genMode> false </genMode>\n    70\t      <needs> .List </needs>\n    71\t      <strictDecode> false </strictDecode>   // true for the ZKIR-EXT surface (canonical-form check on decoding)\n    72\t      <status> ok() </status>\n    73\t    </zkir>\n    74\t\n    75\t  // Generation mode (test harness only): a transcript that runs out yields the\n    76\t  // type's default value and records what was needed; impact values and the\n    77\t  // communications commitment are recorded instead of checked. The harness\n    78\t  // (tools/diff_test.py) uses this to build a consistent preimage before the\n    79\t  // real run.\n    80\t  syntax Need ::= needPubOut(IrType) [symbol(needPubOut)]\n    81\t                | needPriv(IrType)   [symbol(needPriv)]\n    82\t                | needPubIn(Int)     [symbol(needPubIn)]\n    83\t                | needComm(Int)      [symbol(needComm)]\n    84\t  rule <k> genJob(P, Pre) => job(P, Pre) ... </k> <genMode> _ => true </genMode>\n    85\t\n    86\t  // --- Start: decode inputs, seed the public-input vector ------------------------------\n    87\t  rule <k> job(program(Mi, Ins, Outs, DoComm, Is), Pre) => #loadInputs(decodeInputs(#preInputs(Pre), Ins, 0, Strict)) ~> #seedPi ~> Is ~> #verdicts </k>\n    88\t       <pre> _ => Pre </pre> <strictDecode> Strict </strictDecode>\n    89\t       <chips> _ => usedChips(program(Mi, Ins, Outs, DoComm, Is)) </chips>\n    90\t       <outTypes> _ => Outs </outTypes>\n    91\t       <doComm> _ => DoComm </doComm>\n    92\t\n    93\t  syntax List ::= #preInputs(Preimage) [function, total]\n    94\t  rule #preInputs(preimage(I, _, _, _, _, _)) => I\n    95\t  syntax Int ::= #preBinding(Preimage) [function, total]\n    96\t  rule #preBinding(preimage(_, B, _, _, _, _)) => B\n    97\t  syntax CommOpt ::= #preComm(Preimage) [function, total]\n    98\t  rule #preComm(preimage(_, _, C, _, _, _)) => C\n    99\t  syntax List ::= #prePrivate(Preimage) [function, total]\n   100\t  rule #prePrivate(preimage(_, _, _, P, _, _)) => P\n   101\t  syntax List ::= #prePubIn(Preimage) [function, total]\n   102\t  rule #prePubIn(preimage(_, _, _, _, P, _)) => P\n   103\t  syntax List ::= #prePubOut(Preimage) [function, total]\n   104\t  rule #prePubOut(preimage(_, _, _, _, _, P)) => P\n   105\t\n   106\t  syntax KItem ::= #loadInputs(DecodeMany) | \"#seedPi\" | #bind(List)\n   107\t  rule <k> #loadInputs(decManyErr(S)) => .K ... </k> <status> ok() => error(S) </status>\n   108\t  rule <k> #loadInputs(decManyOk(L)) => #bind(L) ... </k>\n   109\t  rule <k> #bind(.List) => .K ... </k>\n   110\t  rule <k> #bind(ListItem(binding(N, V)) L) => #bind(L) ... </k> <mem> M => M[N <- V] </mem>\n   111\t\n   112\t  // pis = [binding_input] ++ [commitment if do_communications_commitment]\n   113\t  rule <k> #seedPi => .K ... </k> <pre> Pre </pre> <doComm> false </doComm>\n   114\t       <pi> _ => ListItem(#preBinding(Pre)) </pi>\n   115\t       <constraints> Cs => Cs ListItem(piFixed(0, var(\"$binding\"))) </constraints>\n   116\t  rule <k> #seedPi => .K ... </k> <pre> Pre </pre> <doComm> true </doComm>\n   117\t       <pi> _ => ListItem(#preBinding(Pre)) ListItem(#commValue(#preComm(Pre))) </pi>\n   118\t       <constraints> Cs => Cs ListItem(piFixed(0, var(\"$binding\"))) ListItem(piFixed(1, var(\"$commitment\"))) </constraints>\n   119\t       <status> St => #requireComm(#preComm(Pre), St) </status>\n   120\t  syntax Int ::= #commValue(CommOpt) [function, total]\n   121\t  rule #commValue(comm(C, _)) => C\n   122\t  rule #commValue(noComm()) => 0\n   123\t  syntax Status ::= #requireComm(CommOpt, Status) [function, total]\n   124\t  rule #requireComm(noComm(), ok()) => error(\"Expected communications commitment\")\n   125\t  rule #requireComm(_, St) => St [owise]\n   126\t\n   127\t  // --- Instruction sequencing ------------------------------------------------------------\n   128\t  rule <k> (I:Instr ; Is:Instrs) => I ~> Is ... </k>\n   129\t  rule <k> .Instrs => #finish ... </k>\n   130\t\n   131\t  // Every instruction emits its constraint, then runs its witness half (if alive).\n   132\t  // The witness half is written as #exec(I); when the status is an error only\n   133\t  // the constraint half fires.\n   134\t  syntax KItem ::= #exec(Instr)\n   135\t  rule <k> I:Instr => #exec(I) ... </k> <constraints> Cs => Cs #constraintsOf(I) </constraints>\n   136\t    requires notBool isImpact(I)\n   137\t  rule <k> #exec(_) => .K ... </k> <status> error(_) </status>\n   138\t\n   139\t  syntax Bool ::= isImpact(Instr) [function, total]\n   140\t  rule isImpact(impact(_, _)) => true\n   141\t  rule isImpact(_) => false [owise]\n   142\t  syntax List ::= #constraintsOf(Instr) [function, total]\n   143\t  rule #constraintsOf(I) => ListItem(gate(I))\n   144\t\n   145\t  // impact: constraints reference absolute public-input positions, so they\n   146\t  // depend on how many public inputs precede them; with a dead witness the\n   147\t  // count continues from the constraint side (piIdx cell would be needed for\n   148\t  // full independence; here we use the length of <pi>, which is frozen on\n   149\t  // error, plus the impacts seen since). The dead-witness case is tracked by\n   150\t  // <deadPis>.\n   151\t  rule <k> impact(G, Xs) => #exec(impact(G, Xs)) ... </k>\n   152\t       <pi> Pi </pi> <deadPis> D </deadPis>\n   153\t       <constraints> Cs => Cs #piGates(size(Pi) +Int D, G, Xs) </constraints>\n   154\t  syntax List ::= #piGates(Int, Operand, Operands) [function, total]\n   155\t  rule #piGates(_, _, .Operands) => .List\n   156\t  rule #piGates(N, G, (X, Xs)) => ListItem(piGate(N, G, X)) #piGates(N +Int 1, G, Xs)\n   157\t\n   158\t  rule <k> #exec(impact(_, Xs)) => .K ... </k> <status> error(_) </status> <deadPis> D => D +Int lenOperands(Xs) </deadPis>\n   159\t    [priority(30)]\n   160\t\n   161\t  // --- Operand resolution ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   162\t  syntax ValueResult ::= resolve(Operand, Map) [function, total]\n   163\t  rule resolve(imm(I), _) => vOk(native(I))\n   164\t  rule resolve(var(X), M) => vOk({M[X]}:>Value) requires X in_keys(M)\n   165\t  rule resolve(var(X), M) => vErr(\"variable not found: Identifier(\\\"\" +String X +String \"\\\")\") requires notBool X in_keys(M)\n   107\t// SHA-512 (FIPS 180-4), 64-bit words, 80 rounds, 128-byte blocks.\n   108\tmodule ZKIR-SHA512\n   109\t  imports ZKIR-HASH\n   110\t  imports ZKIR-SHA512-CONSTANTS\n   111\t\n   112\t  syntax Int ::= rotr64(Int, Int) [function, total]\n   113\t  rule rotr64(X, N) => ((X >>Int N) |Int (X <<Int (64 -Int N))) &Int #m64\n   114\t  syntax Int ::= add64(Int, Int) [function, total]\n   115\t  rule add64(A, B) => (A +Int B) &Int #m64\n   116\t\n   117\t  syntax Bytes ::= sha512Bytes(Bytes) [function, total]\n   118\t  rule sha512Bytes(M) => #sha512Blocks(#sha512Pad(M), 0, #sha512H0)\n   119\t  syntax Bytes ::= #sha512Pad(Bytes) [function, total]\n   120\t  rule #sha512Pad(M) => padRightBytes(M +Bytes Int2Bytes(1, 128, BE), ((lengthBytes(M) +Int 17 +Int 127) /Int 128) *Int 128 -Int 16, 0) +Bytes Int2Bytes(16, lengthBytes(M) *Int 8, BE)\n   121\t  syntax Bytes ::= #sha512Blocks(Bytes, Int, List) [function, total]\n   122\t  rule #sha512Blocks(P, Off, H) => #sha512Out(H) requires Off >=Int lengthBytes(P)\n   123\t  rule #sha512Blocks(P, Off, H) => #sha512Blocks(P, Off +Int 128, #sha512Compress(#sha512Schedule(substrBytes(P, Off, Off +Int 128), 0, .List), H))\n   124\t    requires Off <Int lengthBytes(P)\n   125\t  syntax Bytes ::= #sha512Out(List) [function, total]\n   126\t  rule #sha512Out(.List) => .Bytes\n   127\t  rule #sha512Out(ListItem(W) Ws) => Int2Bytes(8, W, BE) +Bytes #sha512Out(Ws)\n   128\t  syntax List ::= #sha512Schedule(Bytes, Int, List) [function, total]\n   129\t  rule #sha512Schedule(B, T, W) => #sha512Schedule(B, T +Int 1, W ListItem(Bytes2Int(substrBytes(B, 8 *Int T, 8 *Int T +Int 8), BE, Unsigned)))\n   130\t    requires T <Int 16\n   131\t  rule #sha512Schedule(B, T, W) => #sha512Schedule(B, T +Int 1, W ListItem(add64(add64(#t1({W[T -Int 2]}:>Int), {W[T -Int 7]}:>Int), add64(#t0({W[T -Int 15]}:>Int), {W[T -Int 16]}:>Int))))\n   132\t    requires T >=Int 16 andBool T <Int 80\n   133\t  rule #sha512Schedule(_, T, W) => W requires T >=Int 80\n   134\t  syntax Int ::= #t0(Int) [function, total]\n   135\t  rule #t0(X) => rotr64(X, 1) xorInt rotr64(X, 8) xorInt (X >>Int 7)\n   136\t  syntax Int ::= #t1(Int) [function, total]\n   137\t  rule #t1(X) => rotr64(X, 19) xorInt rotr64(X, 61) xorInt (X >>Int 6)\n   138\t  syntax Int ::= #T0(Int) [function, total]\n   139\t  rule #T0(X) => rotr64(X, 28) xorInt rotr64(X, 34) xorInt rotr64(X, 39)\n   140\t  syntax Int ::= #T1(Int) [function, total]\n   141\t  rule #T1(X) => rotr64(X, 14) xorInt rotr64(X, 18) xorInt rotr64(X, 41)\n   142\t  syntax List ::= #sha512Compress(List, List) [function, total]\n   143\t  rule #sha512Compress(W, H) => #sha512AddH(#sha512Round(W, 0, H), H)\n   144\t  syntax List ::= #sha512Round(List, Int, List) [function, total]\n   145\t  rule #sha512Round(_, T, V) => V requires T >=Int 80\n   146\t  rule #sha512Round(W, T, ListItem(A) ListItem(B) ListItem(C) ListItem(D) ListItem(E) ListItem(F) ListItem(G) ListItem(HH))\n   147\t    => #sha512Round(W, T +Int 1, #sha512Next(A, B, C, D, E, F, G,\n   148\t         add64(add64(add64(add64(HH, #T1(E)), (E &Int F) xorInt ((E xorInt #m64) &Int G)), {#sha512Ks[T]}:>Int), {W[T]}:>Int),\n   149\t         add64(#T0(A), (A &Int B) xorInt (A &Int C) xorInt (B &Int C))))\n   150\t    requires T <Int 80\n   151\t  syntax List ::= #sha512Next(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n   152\t  rule #sha512Next(A, B, C, D, E, F, G, T1, T2)\n   153\t    => ListItem(add64(T1, T2)) ListItem(A) ListItem(B) ListItem(C) ListItem(add64(D, T1)) ListItem(E) ListItem(F) ListItem(G)\n   154\t  syntax List ::= #sha512AddH(List, List) [function, total]\n   155\t  rule #sha512AddH(.List, .List) => .List\n   156\t  rule #sha512AddH(ListItem(X) Xs, ListItem(Y) Ys) => ListItem(add64(X, Y)) #sha512AddH(Xs, Ys)\n   157\t  rule #sha512AddH(_, _) => .List [owise]\n   158\tendmodule\n   159\t\n   160\tmodule ZKIR-EXT\nrg: /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_build/ledger-92e8bdd3/zkir*/src/bin/zkir-oracle.rs: IO error for operation on /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_build/ledger-92e8bdd3/zkir*/src/bin/zkir-oracle.rs: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n    62\t    /// Create a new hash-to-curve gadget.\n    63\t    pub fn new(sponge_chip: &H, ecc_chip: &E) -> Self {\n    64\t        Self {\n    65\t            sponge_chip: sponge_chip.clone(),\n    66\t            ecc_chip: ecc_chip.clone(),\n    67\t            _marker: PhantomData,\n    68\t        }\n    69\t    }\n    70\t}\n    71\t\n    72\timpl<F, C, I, H, E> HashToCurveCPU<C, I::Element> for HashToCurveGadget<F, C, I, H, E>\n    73\twhere\n    74\t    F: CircuitField,\n    75\t    C: CircuitCurve + MapToCurveCPU<C>,\n    76\t    I: InnerValue,\n    77\t    H: SpongeInstructions<F, I, E::Coordinate>,\n    78\t    E: EccInstructions<F, C> + MapToCurveInstructions<F, C>,\n    79\t{\n    80\t    fn hash_to_curve(inputs: &[I::Element]) -> C::CryptographicGroup {\n    81\t        let mut state = <H as SpongeCPU<I::Element, C::Base>>::init(None);\n    82\t        <H as SpongeCPU<I::Element, C::Base>>::absorb(&mut state, inputs);\n    83\t        let x1 = <H as SpongeCPU<I::Element, C::Base>>::squeeze(&mut state);\n    84\t        let x2 = <H as SpongeCPU<I::Element, C::Base>>::squeeze(&mut state);\n    85\t        let p1 = C::map_to_curve(&x1);\n    86\t        let p2 = C::map_to_curve(&x2);\n    87\t        p1 + p2\n    88\t    }\n    89\t}\n    90\t\n    91\timpl<F, C, I, H, E> HashToCurveInstructions<F, C, I, E> for HashToCurveGadget<F, C, I, H, E>\n    92\twhere\n    93\t    F: CircuitField,\n    94\t    C: CircuitCurve + MapToCurveCPU<C>,\n    95\t    I: InnerValue,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
