named, typed circuit inputs (decoded from the preimage's\n219:raw `inputs` stream, §6.2). `outputs` declares the positional types the circuit\n236:The preimage must supply exactly one raw field element for `%x` (the encoded\n237:width of `Native`, §4.1). With an empty public transcript, the binding input is\n243:Thirteen types (`ir_types.rs`, `IrType`), each with a fixed raw-`Fr` encoding\n248:| `Native` | `Scalar<BLS12-381>` | 1 | native field element (also Jubjub base field) |\n249:| `Bytes32` | `Bytes<32>` | 2 | 32 bytes |\n251:| `JubjubScalar` | `Scalar<Jubjub>` | 1 | Jubjub scalar field element |\n253:| `Secp256k1Base` | `Base<Secp256k1>` | 2 | Secp256k1 base field element ‡ |\n254:| `Secp256k1Scalar` | `Scalar<Secp256k1>` | 2 | Secp256k1 scalar field element ‡ |\n256:| `Secp256r1Base` | `Base<Secp256r1>` | 2 | Secp256r1 base field element ‡ |\n257:| `Secp256r1Scalar` | `Scalar<Secp256r1>` | 2 | Secp256r1 scalar field element ‡ |\n259:| `Curve25519Base` | `Base<Curve25519>` | 2 | Curve25519 base field element ‡ |\n260:| `Curve25519Scalar` | `Scalar<Curve25519>` | 2 | Curve25519 scalar field element ‡ |\n265:field `Fp`, and `Scalar` re-exported from `curve25519_dalek`). Curve25519's\n268:See §9 for the identity-encoding and decode-canonicity caveats.\n289:P.inputs                    : Fr*    -- raw encoding of the typed circuit inputs\n304:    PI[\"inputs — raw encoding of the typed inputs\"]\n353:| Bit/field manipulation | `DivModPowerOfTwo`, `ReconstituteField` |\n355:| Type conversion | `IntoCoordinates`, `FromCoordinates`, `IntoBytes32`, `FromBytes32`, `ReverseBytes`, `Bytes32IntoLowHigh`, `Bytes32FromLowHigh`, `JubjubScalarFromNative` |\n363:`Native` scalars constrained to `{0, 1}` by convention and, where required for\n376:The thirteen types of §2.2. `Native` is the native (BLS12-381 scalar) field\n377:and the base field of Jubjub. Jubjub is a twisted Edwards curve embedded over\n378:`Native`; Secp256k1 (\"K256\") and Secp256r1 (\"P256\") are Weierstrass c