e, 250s\nexit=0\nPASS  f02_assert_non_boolean                     Finding 2            K=error    Rust=error  gate=assert:holds\n        off-circuit demands cond == 1, the circuit only cond != 0\n        K: Expected boolean, found: 2 | Rust: Expected boolean, found: 02\nPASS  f03_guard_uncoupled                        Finding 3            K=ok       Rust=ok     gate=public_input:holds\n        an inactive guard yields the default value off-circuit; the gate never mentions the guard\n        K: ok | Rust: ok\nPASS  f04_less_than_odd_bits                     Finding 4            K=error    Rust=error  gate=less_than:unknown\n        a = 8 exceeds 3 bits off-circuit; the chip would accept the padded 4-bit bound (output absent, so unknown)\n        K: unknown: register %lt is not in the witness | Rust: Bit bound failed: 08 is not 3-bit\nPASS  f05_noncanonical_foreign_limbs             Finding 5            K=ok       Rust=ok     gate=add:holds\n        limbs encoding p + 5 decode (reduced) as 5 on both sides\n        K: ok | Rust: ok\nPASS  f06_cond_select_bytes32                    Finding 6            K=ok       Rust=ok     gate=cond_select:synthErr\n        cond_select on Bytes32 is accepted off-circuit but has no in-circuit arm\n        K: synthErr: Unsupported cond_select: Bytes32 ? Bytes32 | Rust: ok\nPASS  f07_constrain_eq_jubjub_scalar             Finding 7            K=ok       Rust=ok     gate=constrain_eq:synthErr\n        constrain_eq on JubjubScalar is accepted off-circuit but has no in-circuit arm\n        K: synthErr: Unsupported constrain_eq: JubjubScalar == JubjubScalar | Rust: ok\nPASS  f08_bytes32_from_low_high_foreign_high     Finding 8            K=ok       Rust=ok     gate=bytes32_from_low_high:synthErr\n        a foreign high operand is accepted off-circuit, the circuit requires Native\n        K: synthErr: bytes32_from_low_high high: cannot convert Secp256k1Base to Native | Rust: ok\nPASS  f10_reconstitute_bits_256                  Finding 10           K=wfError  Rust=error  gate=reconstitute_field:n/a\n# k-rust compatibility attempt, 2026-09-05\n\nk-rust 0.4.0 built from repos/midnightntwrk/k-rust (687ccd0) with cargo build --release -p k-rust (4m35s).\n\n1. krust krun toolchain-check/lesson-02-a.k --main-module LESSON-02-A --sort Color -e 'colorOf(Banana())': exit 0 in 2.9 s, result Yellow.\n2. krust kast semantics/zkir-syntax.k --module ZKIR-SYNTAX --sort IrType --expression 'native()': exit 0 in 3.5 s, result `Native`(.KList).\n3. krust krun semantics/zkir.k --main-module ZKIR --sort Job -e '<job term of test_minimal_proof>': no result within the 10-minute tool limit; killed.\n4. timeout 1500 krust kcompile semantics/zkir.k --main-module ZKIR --syntax-module ZKIR-VM-SYNTAX: exit 124 (timed out after 25 minutes, 17+ minutes CPU, ~105 MB RSS, no output, no KORE emitted).\n\nVerdict: the k-rust frontend accepts the definition's syntax but does not finish compiling the full definition in 25 minutes; canonical K compiles it in 20 s.\n     1\t// This file is part of MIDNIGHT-ZK.\n     2\t// Copyright (C) Midnight Foundation\n     3\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n     4\t// Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n     5\t// You may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n     6\t// You may obtain a copy of the License at\n     7\t// http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n     8\t// Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n     9\t// distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n    10\t// WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n    11\t// See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n    12\t// limitations under the License.\n    13\t\n    14\t//! Constants for using Poseidon with the BLS scalar field.\n    15\t//!\n    16\t//! The constants can be reproduced by running the following Sage script from\n    17\t//! [this repository](https://github.